# Brand Colors (Mandatory)

Use ONLY these four brand colors. Do not introduce other hex values for UI styling.

| Name | Hex | Tailwind class |
|------|-----|----------------|
| Navy | `#0B1849` | `bg-brand-navy`, `text-brand-navy`, `border-brand-navy` |
| Green | `#124D1C` | `bg-brand-green`, `text-brand-green`, `border-brand-green` |
| Gold | `#E4B028` | `bg-brand-gold`, `text-brand-gold`, `border-brand-gold` |
| Cream | `#EBEDE3` | `bg-brand-cream`, `text-brand-cream`, `border-brand-cream` |

## Semantic tokens (preferred)

Use theme tokens from `resources/css/app.css` instead of raw hex:

- `bg-background` / `text-foreground` — cream background, navy text (light mode)
- `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` — navy buttons, cream text
- `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary-foreground` — green elements
- `bg-accent` / `text-accent-foreground` — gold highlights
- `ring-ring` — gold focus rings

## TypeScript

Import from `@/lib/brand-colors` when a JS color value is required.

## Rules

- Never hardcode colors outside the palette (except `destructive` for errors).
- Never use Tailwind default colors (`blue-500`, `gray-200`, etc.) for UI.
- Prefer semantic classes (`bg-primary`) over brand classes (`bg-brand-navy`).
